From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Fri, 04 Sep 2026 16:51:23 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-media: request non-coherent (cacheable) host MMAP
 buffers

The host side of a USERPTR session owns vb2 MMAP buffers and copies every
decoded frame out of one into the guest's pages. A coherent dma-contig
MMAP buffer is Normal-NC on arm64, and the CPU reads it at bus speed:
678 MB/s on RPi4 against 3469 MB/s for cached memory, so the 942 KB
RGBA frame costs 1.4 ms instead of 0.3 ms. perf attributes
10.7 % of the device model's CPU to that memcpy.

Pass V4L2_MEMORY_FLAG_NON_COHERENT on the host REQBUFS. vb2 allocates
cacheable memory and does the cache maintenance itself in buf_prepare and
buf_finish; a driver that has not set allow_cache_hints clears the flag,
so the log line reports whether it stuck. bcm2835-codec gets the flag in
the DomD kernel patch 0015.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [depends on the downstream virtio-media device
 (0216), which upstream qemu does not have]
---
diff --git a/hw/virtio/virtio-media.c b/hw/virtio/virtio-media.c
index 5d79cd3af62..05c07de67b0 100644
--- a/hw/virtio/virtio-media.c
+++ b/hw/virtio/virtio-media.c
@@ -662,6 +662,16 @@ static int virtio_media_reqbufs(VirtIOMediaSession *s,
      * carries whatever its own header version put there.
      */
     memset(host_rb.reserved, 0, sizeof(host_rb.reserved));
+    /*
+     * Ask for cacheable host buffers. A coherent vb2 MMAP buffer is Normal-NC
+     * on arm64 and this device reads every decoded frame out of one with the
+     * CPU: 678 MB/s against 3469 MB/s for cached memory on RPi4, 1.4 ms per
+     * 942 KB frame instead of 0.3 ms (perf: 10 % of the device model's CPU).
+     * vb2 honours the flag only if the driver sets allow_cache_hints, and
+     * clears it otherwise, so on a driver without it nothing changes; the
+     * cache maintenance then happens in vb2's buf_prepare/buf_finish.
+     */
+    host_rb.flags = V4L2_MEMORY_FLAG_NON_COHERENT;
     if (ioctl(s->fd, VIDIOC_REQBUFS, &host_rb) < 0) {
         int err = errno;
         struct v4l2_format fmt = { .type = rb->type };
@@ -682,8 +692,10 @@ static int virtio_media_reqbufs(VirtIOMediaSession *s,
         }
         return err;
     }
-    info_report("virtio-media: host REQBUFS type=%u -> count=%u caps=0x%x (fd %d)",
-                host_rb.type, host_rb.count, host_rb.capabilities, s->fd);
+    info_report("virtio-media: host REQBUFS type=%u -> count=%u caps=0x%x "
+                "non_coherent=%u (fd %d)", host_rb.type, host_rb.count,
+                host_rb.capabilities,
+                !!(host_rb.flags & V4L2_MEMORY_FLAG_NON_COHERENT), s->fd);
     if (host_rb.count > VIRTIO_MEDIA_MAX_BUFFERS) {
         /*
          * Give the surplus back rather than silently tracking fewer buffers
